# Cathedral Marquise Engagement Ring ({{year}}): 3 Snag Risks That Multiply

![Three loose marquise cut diamonds held in jeweller tweezers against a soft grey backdrop as the DiamondCritics featured image for the {{year}} cathedral marquise engagement ring guide titled 3 snag risks that multiply](/images/cathedral-marquise-engagement-ring.jpg "Cathedral Marquise Engagement Ring 3 Snag Risks That Multiply")

## TL;DR — Cathedral Marquise Engagement Ring in One Scroll

**A cathedral marquise engagement ring uses rising cathedral shoulders that lift the centre stone high above the finger** — like the arches of a cathedral framing a stained-glass window. The look is dramatic and architectural. The problem on a marquise is that the cathedral height AND the pointed marquise tips are both snag-prone features. Stack both together and the ring catches on everything from sweaters to car doors to hair ties. Cathedral marquise is beautiful for formal wearers, risky for daily hands-on wearers.

**The 3 snag risks that multiply (all 3 covered in full below):**

- **Risk 1 — Cathedral height + marquise tip length = double-stacked snag surface.** Standard cathedral raises the stone 3–5 mm above the finger. The marquise tip adds another 1–2 mm reach past the sides. The combination creates two independent snag planes — top-of-stone + side-of-tip.
- **Risk 2 — Pavé-crown cathedrals snag faster than plain cathedrals.** Pavé stones along the cathedral shoulders catch on fibre like velcro. Plain metal cathedral surfaces slide. The pavé-crown aesthetic adds beauty and multiplies snag frequency.
- **Risk 3 — Hands-on lifestyle multiplies snag frequency 5–10x.** Medical workers, cooks, mechanics, teachers, and parents of young children all see 10+ snags per week on cathedral marquise rings. Office workers see fewer than 2 per week. Match setting to lifestyle before you buy.

→ Low-profile pick: **[East West Knife Edge Cathedral Solitaire in 14k White Gold at $975](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/east-west-knife-edge-cathedral-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-311245?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — east-west + low cathedral = minimal snag surface.
