## The Hands-On Lifestyle Test

**The Hands-On Lifestyle Test is the single most important check before buying a cathedral marquise.** Answer three questions honestly before you order:

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Answer "Yes" means</th><th>Cathedral Fit</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Will the wearer use their hands for 4+ hours per day for professional work?</strong></td><td>Hands-on worker</td><td>Avoid cathedral</td><td>Switch to bezel or low-profile solitaire.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Will the wearer regularly handle fabric (towels, bedding, children's clothing, baking)?</strong></td><td>Fabric contact</td><td>Avoid pavé crown</td><td>Low plain cathedral acceptable; skip pavé.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Will the wearer regularly wear gloves (medical, construction, winter sports)?</strong></td><td>Glove-dependent</td><td>Avoid cathedral entirely</td><td>Glove-pull multiplies cathedral snag 10x+.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Office worker, formal wear only, careful with hands?</strong></td><td>Low-contact wearer</td><td>Cathedral works great</td><td>Any cathedral height + pavé fine.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** If any of the first three questions is "yes," cathedral marquise is the wrong setting for daily wear. Pick bezel for max durability or low-profile solitaire for subtle elegance. If all three answers are "no," cathedral marquise fits beautifully.

